  "notes": [
   "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
   "Top rails: tp is the + (5V) rail and tn the GND rail; bottom rails bp (+) and bn (GND) are tied to them by wire9 and wire8.",
   "Each FSR forms a voltage divider: one lead to the + rail, the other lead to the analog-pin column, and a 10K resistor from that column to the GND rail. The image shows the A0 wire going to column 16 and the A1 wire to column 6, so fsr1/r1/wire6 sit at column 16 and fsr2/r2/wire7 at column 6.",
   "Pushbutton: side 1 (column 5, top and bottom halves) is wired to 5V. Side 2 (column 7) goes to pin 2, and the 10K pull-down r3 runs from column 7 to the GND strip at column 10. Pressing joins 5V to pin 2. The image has the button joined pairs running across the centre gap, so 1.l/1.r take the column 5 holes and 2.l/2.r the column 7 holes.",
   "Sensor lead-to-hole assignments follow the image's approximate column positions; the FSR legs are symmetric."
  ]
 },
